WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.730
<v Narrator>Two days before a visit, Contoso Health calls each patient with a reminder.

2
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:12.733
<v Narrator>A recording reads the visit to whoever picks up, and any change means calling back.

3
00:00:12.813 --> 00:00:16.530
<v Narrator>This agent checks it's Jordan first, then settles it on the call.

4
00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:25.880
<v Narrator>Your server decides who to call, and when.

5
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:30.820
<v Narrator>Then Azure Communication Services Call Automation dials from the clinic's number.

6
00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:34.613
<v Narrator>Voice Live, with GPT Realtime, holds the conversation,

7
00:00:34.693 --> 00:00:39.110
<v Narrator>while your reminder policy decides what may be said and what may change.

8
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:43.095
<v Narrator>New times go to the scheduling desk in Teams, with context.

9
00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:47.870
<v Narrator>Patients who call back on the clinic's Teams Phone number reach the same agent.

10
00:00:50.282 --> 00:00:54.132
<v Narrator>Ten in the morning, two days before Jordan's imaging visit.

11
00:00:54.212 --> 00:00:59.432
<v Narrator>Before dialing, the server checks consent, calling hours and the reminder window.

12
00:01:00.455 --> 00:01:01.205
<v Jordan>Hello?

13
00:01:01.285 --> 00:01:04.327
<v Agent>Hi, this is Contoso Health's automated assistant,

14
00:01:04.407 --> 00:01:06.793
<v Agent>calling with an appointment reminder.

15
00:01:06.873 --> 00:01:08.735
<v Agent>Am I speaking with Jordan?

16
00:01:10.053 --> 00:01:11.753
<v Jordan>Yes, this is Jordan.

17
00:01:12.102 --> 00:01:16.582
<v Agent>Thanks, Jordan. To protect your privacy, please tell me your date of birth.

18
00:01:17.907 --> 00:01:19.877
<v Narrator>A name is a claim, not proof.

19
00:01:19.957 --> 00:01:23.754
<v Narrator>Until the date of birth matches a record the model never sees,

20
00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:26.327
<v Narrator>every appointment tool stays blocked.

21
00:01:27.164 --> 00:01:29.664
<v Jordan>March 12th, 1984.

22
00:01:29.977 --> 00:01:32.834
<v Agent>You have an imaging appointment with Dr.

23
00:01:32.914 --> 00:01:36.994
<v Agent>Lee on Thursday, May 21 at 9:30 AM, at the Northgate clinic.

24
00:01:37.074 --> 00:01:39.277
<v Agent>Will you be able to make it?

25
00:01:40.632 --> 00:01:43.522
<v Narrator>It matched, so only now does the visit come up.

26
00:01:43.602 --> 00:01:48.192
<v Narrator>Only an explicit yes confirms it, and the server writes that to the schedule.

27
00:01:49.058 --> 00:01:50.658
<v Jordan>Yes, I'll be there.

28
00:01:50.972 --> 00:01:52.305
<v Agent>You're confirmed.

29
00:01:52.385 --> 00:01:53.718
<v Agent>Please do not eat

30
00:01:53.798 --> 00:01:57.958
<v Agent>or drink anything except water for 8 hours before your appointment,

31
00:01:58.038 --> 00:02:01.712
<v Agent>and arrive 15 minutes early. We'll see you then. Goodbye.

32
00:02:03.046 --> 00:02:06.300
<v Narrator>The prep instructions come from config, not the model.

33
00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:11.166
<v Narrator>And the trail shows the order: identity verified, details shared, then confirmed.

34
00:02:13.218 --> 00:02:16.626
<v Narrator>Every missed visit is a slot another patient could have had.

35
00:02:16.706 --> 00:02:18.758
<v Narrator>Avery Stone can't make this one.

36
00:02:19.782 --> 00:02:21.012
<v Avery>I need to cancel.

37
00:02:21.322 --> 00:02:26.599
<v Agent>I can cancel your primary care appointment on Thursday, May 21 at 10:15 AM.

38
00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:28.422
<v Agent>Should I cancel it?

39
00:02:29.784 --> 00:02:32.232
<v Narrator>That's a proposal, not a cancellation.

40
00:02:32.312 --> 00:02:37.094
<v Narrator>It's read back, and the schedule stays as it was until Avery gives a clear yes.

41
00:02:37.936 --> 00:02:39.986
<v Avery>Yes, please cancel it.

42
00:02:40.289 --> 00:02:47.119
<v Agent>Your appointment is cancelled, and the time is now open for another patient.

43
00:02:47.199 --> 00:02:52.299
<v Agent>To book a new visit, call us at 206-555-0100. Goodbye.

44
00:02:53.666 --> 00:02:58.106
<v Narrator>Dr. Patel's ten-fifteen is open again, with two days left to fill it.

45
00:03:00.154 --> 00:03:01.958
<v Narrator>Riley wants a different time.

46
00:03:02.038 --> 00:03:04.403
<v Narrator>The agent has no tool that can book one.

47
00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:06.214
<v Narrator>That's a job for a person.

48
00:03:07.168 --> 00:03:08.855
<v Narrator>Because Riley is verified,

49
00:03:08.935 --> 00:03:13.198
<v Narrator>the server may hand the call to a person at the scheduling desk, in Teams.

50
00:03:14.062 --> 00:03:15.652
<v Riley>Can I come next week instead?

51
00:03:15.972 --> 00:03:19.338
<v Agent>I'll connect you with our scheduling team to find a new time.

52
00:03:19.418 --> 00:03:23.712
<v Agent>Your current appointment stays booked until you choose a new one. Please hold.

53
00:03:25.059 --> 00:03:29.097
<v Narrator>Before anyone picks up, the scheduler sees who's calling and why.

54
00:03:29.177 --> 00:03:31.523
<v Narrator>That context rides in VoIP headers,

55
00:03:31.603 --> 00:03:36.059
<v Narrator>with a single-use patient reference: no date of birth, no phone number.

56
00:03:38.158 --> 00:03:40.857
<v Narrator>Anyone in the house can play back a voicemail.

57
00:03:40.937 --> 00:03:43.768
<v Narrator>This is the third and last try to reach Camila.

58
00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:47.615
<v Narrator>Call Automation has no answering-machine detection,

59
00:03:47.695 --> 00:03:52.000
<v Narrator>so the server judges the greeting itself: its words, its length, a beep.

60
00:03:52.956 --> 00:03:54.419
<v Camila's voicemail>Hi, you've reached Camila.

61
00:03:54.499 --> 00:03:56.586
<v Camila's voicemail>Please leave a message after the tone.

62
00:03:56.849 --> 00:04:02.346
<v Agent>This is Contoso Health calling for Camila with an appointment reminder.

63
00:04:02.426 --> 00:04:06.309
<v Agent>Please call us back at 602-555-0100. Thank you.

64
00:04:07.652 --> 00:04:11.031
<v Narrator>A first name and a callback number, nothing about the visit.

65
00:04:11.111 --> 00:04:13.552
<v Narrator>Earlier tries hang up without a message.

66
00:04:15.624 --> 00:04:20.434
<v Narrator>Now it's eight-thirty in the evening, and Noah Martin is still due a reminder.

67
00:04:22.984 --> 00:04:26.076
<v Narrator>The server checks calling hours in Noah's own time zone.

68
00:04:26.156 --> 00:04:29.874
<v Narrator>Too late, so nothing is dialed, and the model never hears about it.

69
00:04:32.281 --> 00:04:35.422
<v Narrator>Every call is audited, even the ones never placed,

70
00:04:35.502 --> 00:04:38.001
<v Narrator>and the same log feeds these numbers.

71
00:04:39.637 --> 00:04:43.533
<v Narrator>A date of birth is a knowledge check, not strong authentication.

72
00:04:43.613 --> 00:04:46.846
<v Narrator>So it grants very little: one appointment's details,

73
00:04:46.926 --> 00:04:49.797
<v Narrator>and a confirm or a cancel after a clear yes.

74
00:04:50.247 --> 00:04:53.330
<v Narrator>And the model cannot dial, transfer or book.

75
00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:57.607
<v Narrator>Phone numbers, Teams IDs and times all come from your server.

76
00:04:59.807 --> 00:05:03.755
<v Narrator>Making it yours starts in config: the reminder window, calling hours,

77
00:05:03.835 --> 00:05:07.497
<v Narrator>every line the server says, and each clinic's callback number.

78
00:05:07.947 --> 00:05:10.181
<v Narrator>Then point the desk at your Teams user,

79
00:05:10.261 --> 00:05:13.707
<v Narrator>and have your coding agent connect your own scheduling system.

80
00:05:16.307 --> 00:05:17.827
<v Narrator>Appointment Reminder Agent.

81
00:05:17.907 --> 00:05:19.839
<v Narrator>Run it in simulation in two minutes,

82
00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:23.257
<v Narrator>then connect your clinic's number and your Teams scheduling desk.
